It was pouring outside.&nbsp;

Arohi woke up at 7.30 am . Usually she woke up at 7 am but since&nbsp; it was holiday , she slept a little longer. She was a working woman and lived alone in an apartment . She had to prepare herself breakfast but couldn’t decide what to cook. Suddenly an idea popped into her mind .

“ Khichuri.”

“ It will be perfect for today’s weather.”

At first, she freshened up . Then she went to the&nbsp; kitchen and prepared everything. She started cutting the&nbsp; vegetables and washing the rice and lentils . She put a pan on the stove and started cooking.&nbsp;

Suddenly she remembered the old days.&nbsp;

On a rainy day , her mother used to cook Khichuri for whole family. She and her brothers waited eagerly in the dining table.&nbsp;

“ Ma , how long we have to wait ?? We are starving. ”

“ wait two minutes, dear .”

“ Ok ”

“ Here your Khichuri, enjoy ! . ”

Her mother served the Khichuri with fried brinjal , potatoes and many other side dishes.&nbsp;

They loved it .&nbsp;

“oh , delicious!”

“ Yummy !”

Arohi suddenly came back to reality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

She served her plain Khichuri in a bowl and looked around at her empty dining space . The apartment was silent. Her&nbsp; heart felt heavy. Tears unconsciously welled up in her eyes…..

She took a spoonful of Khichuri and smiled faintly. Somehow it didn’t taste the same anymore.&nbsp;
